STEP 1 — Environment Setup (10–15 mins)
In Kaggle Notebook:
Enable GPU
Import core libraries:
numpy
pandas
torch
torchvision
cv2 / PIL
Verify GPU is available (torch.cuda.is_available())
👉 If GPU isn’t detected: stop and fix this first

STEP 2 — Understand the Dataset Structure
In the notebook:
List dataset directories
Identify:
CT slices
Ink labels
Tile structure
Print shapes, dtypes, ranges
Do not preprocess yet — just inspect.
👉 Outcome: you know where everything lives.

STEP 3 — Visual Data Inspection
Still in the notebook:
Load one tile
Display:
Several Z-slices
Corresponding ink label
Scroll through depth manually
Focus on:
Where ink appears
How thin / subtle it is
Which Z-range looks informative
👉 Outcome: intuition about the signal.

STEP 4 — Minimal Preprocessing
Implement only:
Min–max normalization (or z-score)
Optional clipping
No filters, no tricks yet.
Test:
Before vs after visually
👉 Outcome: stable, predictable inputs.

STEP 5 — Patch Extraction Logic
In the notebook:
Define patch size (e.g. 256×256)
Define Z-slice depth (e.g. 7–17)
Extract patches:
Near surface
From ink & non-ink areas
Confirm:
Patch shapes
Patch values
Corresponding label patches
👉 Outcome: model-ready inputs.

STEP 6 — Dataset & Dataloader
Implement:
Custom Dataset
DataLoader with:
Batch size that fits GPU
Shuffling for training
Test:
One batch forward pass
Print tensor shapes
👉 Outcome: training loop won’t break later.

STEP 7 — Baseline Model
Use:
Simple UNet
2D or 2.5D (recommended)
Check:
Input channels match Z-slices
Output shape matches mask
Run:
Single forward pass
Outcome: model wiring is correct.

STEP 8 — Training Loop
Implement:
Loss: Dice or Dice + BCE
Optimiser: Adam
Training loop
Validation loop
Save best model
Run:
Short training (even 1–2 epochs)
👉 Outcome: loss decreases, nothing crashes.

STEP 9 — Sliding Window Inference
Implement:
Sliding window over full tile
Overlapping patches
Averaging/blending predictions
Visualise:
Full reconstructed ink probability map
👉 Outcome: you can predict on full data.

STEP 10 — Submission File
Convert predictions into:
Correct shape
Correct format
Correct filename
Submit to Kaggle.

🎉 You are officially competing.

STEP 11 — Verify & Freeze Baseline
Before touching anything:
Note leaderboard score
Save notebook version
Freeze baseline settings

👉 This is your reference point.
